/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Search a 2D Matrix II
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Matrix
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given an m x n matrix where:
- Every row is sorted in ascending order from left to right.
- Every column is sorted in ascending order from top to bottom.

Return true if target exists in the matrix, otherwise false.

Approach:
We start from the TOP-RIGHT corner of the matrix.

Why top-right?

At any position matrix[r][c]:

- Everything to the LEFT is smaller or equal.
- Everything BELOW is greater or equal.

Therefore:

1. If matrix[r][c] == target:
       Target found.

2. If matrix[r][c] > target:
       The current value is too large.
       Since everything BELOW is even larger,
       we cannot move down.
       So move LEFT:
           c--

3. If matrix[r][c] < target:
       The current value is too small.
       Since everything to the LEFT is even smaller,
       we cannot move left.
       So move DOWN:
           r++

This eliminates one complete row or one complete column
at every step.

------------------------------------------------------------
Dry Run
------------------------------------------------------------

Matrix:

    1   4   7   11  15
    2   5   8   12  19
    3   6   9   16  22
    10  13  14  17  24
    18  21  23  26  30

target = 5

Start at top-right:

    15

15 > 5
    Move LEFT

    11

11 > 5
    Move LEFT

    7

7 > 5
    Move LEFT

    4

4 < 5
    Move DOWN

    5

5 == target

Return true.

------------------------------------------------------------
Why top-right works
------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose:

    current = 7
    target = 5

Because rows are sorted:

    values to the left of 7 are smaller
    values to the right of 7 are larger

Because columns are sorted:

    values below 7 are larger

Since 7 > 5:
    - Going right is impossible.
    - Going down is impossible.
    - Only LEFT can contain 5.

Similarly, if:

    current = 4
    target = 5

Since 4 < 5:
    - Going left gives even smaller values.
    - Only DOWN can contain 5.

------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithm
------------------------------------------------------------

1. Check if matrix is empty.
2. Set:
       r = 0
       c = number of columns - 1
3. While r is inside the matrix and c >= 0:
       a. If matrix[r][c] == target -> true
       b. If matrix[r][c] > target -> c--
       c. Otherwise -> r++
4. If the loop ends, target does not exist.
5. Return false.

------------------------------------------------------------
Complexity
------------------------------------------------------------

At every step, either:
    row increases
or
    column decreases.

Maximum number of moves:
    m + n

Time Complexity  : O(m + n)
Space Complexity : O(1)

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    bool searchMatrix(vector<vector<int>>& matrix, int target) {
        // Handle empty matrix
        if (matrix.empty() || matrix[0].empty()) {
            return false;
        }

        int r = 0;
        int c = matrix[0].size() - 1;

        // Start from top-right corner
        while (r < matrix.size() && c >= 0) {

            if (matrix[r][c] == target) {
                return true;
            }

            // Current value is too large
            else if (matrix[r][c] > target) {
                c--;
            }

            // Current value is too small
            else {
                r++;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
};
